3. App Flow
Launch: main.dart initializes Flutter binding and loads the theme preference.
Splash: SplashScreen plays an animation -> auto-navigates to BrowserHomePage.
Home / Browser: BrowserHomePage checks if the current tab is a "Homepage" or a URL.
Homepage State: Shows the Clock, Search Bar, Weather Widget, and App Shortcuts.
Browsing State: Renders an InAppWebView with the current URL.
Navigation: Users can search via the text field, click shortcuts, or use the bottom "AI Menu" / "Google Apps" menu.
Multi-Tab: Clicking the "Tabs" icon opens AllTabsPage to switch contexts.
4. Key Features Implemented
Web Browsing: Full-featured browsing using flutter_inappwebview.
Multi-Tab Support: Create, close, and switch tabs. State is persisted.
Dynamic Weather Widget: Fetches real-time weather (temp, humidity, condition) and changes background/overlay animations (rain, fog, sunny).
History Management: automatically logs visited URLs; allows clearing history.
Custom Shortcuts: Quick access to Google Apps (Drive, Mail, Maps) and AI Tools (ChatGPT, Gemini, Claude).
Extensions: Basic system to inject JavaScript (AdBlocker placeholders exist).
Desktop Mode: Toggle to request desktop sites.
Theming: Light/Dark mode toggles.
5. State Management
Approach: setState (Ephemerial State) The app relies entirely on React-style setState within StatefulWidgets.

Wiring: Data like _tabs, _history, and _weatherCondition are stored as local variables in BrowserHomePageState.
Persistence: Data is manually saved to SharedPreferences via helper classes (TabsManager, HistoryManager) whenever setState modifies it.
6. Routing / Navigation
Approach: Navigator 1.0 (Imperative)

Simple Navigator.push() and Navigator.pop() calls.
Routes are built on the fly using MaterialPageRoute.
Example: Navigator.push(context, MaterialPageRoute(builder: (_) => AllTabsPage(...))).
7. Web Browsing Implementation
Package: flutter_inappwebview

Logic: The BrowserHomePage toggles between a native Flutter view (the custom homepage) and the InAppWebView widget based on the isHomepage flag of the current tab.
Event Handling:
onLoadStop: Updates the history and tab title/favicon.
onProgressChanged: Updates the loading bar (though visual loading bar code seems minimal).
Extensions: ExtensionLoader is designed to run controller.runJavaScript() to inject scripts.
