10. Missing / Incomplete / TODOs
Tab Persistence Bug: While logic exists to save tabs, the InAppWebView state (scroll position, form data) is lost when switching tabs because the WebView is often rebuilt or disposed.
Extension Logic: The UI for adding extensions exists, but the "AdBlock" logic is just a placeholder variable (enabled: true) without actual blocking logic implemented.
Search Engine Choice: The UI shows buttons for Google/DuckDuckGo/Bing, but the code largely defaults to Google search strings.
11. Code Smells & Risky Patterns
Duplicate Entry Points: salate_browser.dart contains a full MaterialApp and main function but is likely unused. This confuses the project structure.
Hardcoded API Keys: The WeatherAPI key is committed directly in weather_service.dart.
Monolithic Home Page: home_page.dart is 1,500+ lines long. It handles UI, logic, weather parsing, tab management, and search logic. This violates the "Single Responsibility Principle".
Redundant Dependencies: webview_flutter is listed but flutter_inappwebview is the one actually being used for the main browser.
Mixed UI Logic: BrowserHomePage toggles between "Home" and "WebView" using an if statement in the body. This works but makes the widget tree heavy.
12. Architecture Style
Feature-First / Monolithic It doesn't strictly follow Clean Architecture or MVC. It's a pragmatic, standard Flutter app structure:

pages/ (View)
models/ (Model)
utils/ (Controller/Service combined)
It relies heavily on "Spaghetti Code" in the main home_page.dart rather than separating concerns into distinct logic classes.

